@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace-Conventional/src/laplace_conventional/cli.py SHA256 36d0a136f9cbe4f76c959b641b3d9b2dc676619caa633c1b8724fa8ec11f1359
' Evidence: Laplace-Conventional/src/laplace_conventional/modality_plan.py SHA256 1c1865b3fcc1e01cd010d39fa29c45d53a6b954b668a318cad99568d4006da22
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Conventional — image, audio and video provider plans
start
:Load selected manifest and hardware;
while (Image, audio, video settings remain?) is (yes)
 if (Modality disabled?) then (yes)
  :Record disabled with zero files/bytes;
 else (enabled)
  :Select unique manifest entries matching provider;
  :For audio with video-audio policy, also include selected video containers;
  if (No source entries?) then (yes)
   :Record present=false;
  else (present)
   :Instantiate configured provider model; count parameters and largest layer;
   :Delete model; collect memory;
   :Apply optional modality microbatch override; derive execution plan;
   :If require-fit, validate before adding this plan;
  endif
 endif
endwhile (done)
:Write combined modality plan; print;
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Complete planning module reviewed. Provider candidates are selected from
metadata; video containers without audio are resolved later by training/data code. Model
constructors, media decoding and training acceptance remain nested. Unlike plan-execution
CLI, required fit is checked before writing the combined plan.
end footer

@enduml
